# The build context is the source and nothing else.
#
# .git alone is 1.2 GiB here, and every byte of it is uploaded to the builder
# before the first instruction runs.
.git

# Build output and installed dependencies are REPRODUCED by the build. Sending a
# working tree's copies makes the image depend on the machine that built it —
# and `npm ci` and `go build` would then be layering onto someone else's results.
#
# The platform workspaces are the half this used to miss, and it does not fail
# quietly. `npm ci` runs the root postinstall, which builds all four of them, so
# a stale .rollup.cache reaches rollup-plugin-ts and it hands rollup untouched
# TSX:
#
#   src/index.tsx (5:7) Unexpected token
#   (Note that you need plugins to import files that are not JavaScript)
#
# tsbuildinfo does the same to tsc more politely — "Project is up to date" over
# sources the image has never compiled. Both only happen when the tree was built
# in before the image was, so CI never sees either and a developer sees both.
**/node_modules
webapp/channels/dist
webapp/platform/*/dist
webapp/platform/*/lib
webapp/**/.rollup.cache
webapp/.parcel-cache
webapp/**/*.tsbuildinfo
